      "expected": "{\"asOf\":\"2026-07-16T00:00:00Z\",\"assurance\":\"wallet-signature-only\",\"claimedClass\":\"TC-2\",\"coverage\":{\"bindings\":[\"evm:x402\"],\"ports\":[\"evm\"]},\"settlements\":{\"found\":[{\"chainId\":84532,\"txHash\":\"0x11\"}],\"multiplySettled\":false},\"steps\":[{\"name\":\"atr-fingerprint\",\"outcome\":{\"status\":\"proved\"}},{\"name\":\"buyer-acceptance\",\"outcome\":{\"depth\":\"no-buyer-port\",\"status\":\"not-attempted\"}},{\"name\":\"authority-attenuation\",\"outcome\":{\"haltClass\":\"verification-failure\",\"status\":\"failed\"}}],\"supportedClass\":\"TC-0\",\"verified\":false}",
      "$comment": "A report whose authority-attenuation step FAILED. supportedClass is TC-0 — any failed step impeaches, whatever else proved — while claimedClass keeps the TC-2 the record was shaped for, so the divergence between the two is legible. Expected re-derived from the RFC 8785 sort by an independent implementation, not copied from the emitter. SUPERSEDES the pin taken when supportedClass echoed the claim and read TC-2 over a failed step: {\"asOf\":\"2026-07-16T00:00:00Z\",\"assurance\":\"wallet-signature-only\",\"coverage\":{\"bindings\":[\"evm:x402\"],\"ports\":[\"evm\"]},\"settlements\":{\"found\":[{\"chainId\":84532,\"txHash\":\"0x11\"}],\"multiplySettled\":false},\"steps\":[{\"name\":\"atr-fingerprint\",\"outcome\":{\"status\":\"proved\"}},{\"name\":\"buyer-acceptance\",\"outcome\":{\"depth\":\"no-buyer-port\",\"status\":\"not-attempted\"}},{\"name\":\"authority-attenuation\",\"outcome\":{\"haltClass\":\"verification-failure\",\"status\":\"failed\"}}],\"supportedClass\":\"TC-2\",\"verified\":false}"
    },
